WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.600
T5.

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.680
One model, one format, every language task.

3
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.167
Let's see how it works.

4
00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:10.300
T5 stands for Text-to-Text Transfer Transformer.

5
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:17.633
Translation, summarization, classification, even regression: all become input text to output text.

6
00:00:17.933 --> 00:00:20.667
And the task itself is stated inside the input.

7
00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:23.133
Here is the pipeline.

8
00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:26.267
The input starts with a task prefix, then the text.

9
00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.900
The encoder reads it in both directions.

10
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.116
The decoder writes the answer through cross-attention.

11
00:00:32.116 --> 00:00:33.467
That's the output string.

12
00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.800
Look at three prompts on the same log line.

13
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.467
Start with summarize, and you get a summary.

14
00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:42.667
Start with translate to German, and you get German.

15
00:00:42.967 --> 00:00:46.367
Ask whether it is routine or critical, and you get triage.

16
00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:48.900
Notice what that means.

17
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.300
If the task lives in the input, changing behavior means changing text, not weights.

18
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.533
That is prompting, two years early.

19
00:00:57.733 --> 00:00:59.500
Here is Flan-T5 in code.

20
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.400
We load a single small model.

21
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:04.748
Then we call it three times with different wording.

22
00:01:04.748 --> 00:01:06.600
Same weights, zero fine-tuning.

23
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.500
Not every alert deserves a frontier model call.

24
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:18.367
Flan-T5 runs on CPU as tier one, summarizing and triaging every notice, sub-second and nearly free.

25
00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.533
Only critical alerts escalate.

26
00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:23.409
The big LLM writes the full analysis.

27
00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:27.933
This two-tier pattern cuts the API bill by an order of magnitude.

28
00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:29.970
Let's recap.

29
00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:32.200
Every task is text in, text out.

30
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.733
One encoder-decoder handles them all.

31
00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:37.000
You change the prompt, not the weights.

32
00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:40.679
And Flan-T5 is a cheap CPU workhorse.

33
00:01:40.679 --> 00:01:41.867
Next up: GPT.
